{"claims":[
{"text":"The rider's own chat log defeats any exoneration under POL-NS-04. MSG-00604-002, her coordinating message naming the block ('my dad cannot walk, pls come to the block pickup bay Blk 185'), was sent at 09:45:50, and the driver answered at 09:46:20 - thirty seconds later, well inside the 120 second window POL-NS-04(b) allows. The clause says in terms that where the driver did reply within 120 seconds it does not apply 'regardless of the content of the reply', so limb (b) fails on the face of the log and the rider cannot claim the no-compensation exoneration that route offers her.","evidence_ids":["EV-CHAT-00604","EV-TRIP-00604"],"clause_ids":["POL-NS-04"],"relies_on":"EV-CHAT-00604 messages MSG-00604-002 and MSG-00604-003","asserted_weight":1.0},
{"text":"The arrival marker is not a false marker caught by POL-NS-05. Across the entire 67-fix trace the driver's recorded speeds are either 0 km/h or between 4.9 and 8.1 km/h, so the 15 km/h motion trigger is unreachable on this evidence, and his displacement from the pin never leaves the 134.6 m to 302.4 m band - he was in the vicinity of the pickup throughout, with stationary fixes. This is precisely the case POL-NS-05 carves out and sends to POL-NS-03 (a driver outside the arrival radius but nearby when he marks arrival), and the false-arrival entry that POL-NS-05(ii) would write into the referrals list is not available against him.","evidence_ids":["EV-GPS-00604","EV-TRIP-00604"],"clause_ids":["POL-NS-05","POL-NS-03"],"relies_on":"derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph","asserted_weight":1.0},
{"text":"What the trace shows on the ground is a driver who was at the pickup venue but at the wrong face of it, which is the situation POL-NS-03 governs. Sixty-seven fixes with no sampling gap across eleven minutes place him with a nearest approach of 134.6 m and a mean displacement of 205.9 m from the pin - wholly inside POL-NS-03's 400 m ceiling - and that is corroborated by his contemporaneous account that the block road is narrow and blocked by delivery bikes so he stopped at the nearest safe place.","evidence_ids":["EV-GPS-00604","EV-TRIP-00604"],"clause_ids":["POL-NS-03"],"relies_on":"derived.driver_track.mean_distance_m","asserted_weight":1.0},
{"text":"The physical record corroborates the driver's account rather than the hardship narrative: 0.56 km of travel in eleven minutes with every non-zero fix at 4.9 to 8.1 km/h is a carriageway the driver was crawling along, not a driver who declined to attend, and it explains why he never got inside the 50 m geofence before the rider cancelled at 09:51:50. A driver standing off 200 m on a block road he cannot enter is the POL-NS-03 wrong-entrance case, not a fee-farming no-show.","evidence_ids":["EV-GPS-00604","EV-TRIP-00604"],"clause_ids":["POL-NS-03"],"relies_on":"derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph","asserted_weight":1.0},
{"text":"Fault under POL-NS-03 is allocated out of the chat log, and that log holds three civil messages - 'come to main road' at 09:45:10, the rider's request at 09:45:50, and the driver's 'cannot' at 09:46:20 - and nothing in it supports the rider's assertion that the driver 'got rude'. The driver's last word is a plain refusal on grounds of access, and the record does not contain a single abusive or gratuitous message from him.","evidence_ids":["EV-CHAT-00604","EV-TRIP-00604"],"clause_ids":["POL-NS-03"],"relies_on":"EV-CHAT-00604 message_count","asserted_weight":1.0},
{"text":"The driver does not argue that the distance test can be carried: the trace's qualified in-geofence fix count is 0 and his closest fix is 134.6 m from the pin, beyond the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, so POL-NS-01 limb (b) is not made out on this evidence and the fee cannot stand on POL-NS-01. What the record does carry is limb (a), a driver 'arrived' event at 09:44:52, so the case is a wrong-face-of-the-pickup case under POL-NS-03 and not a driver who never attended the venue at all - and POL-NS-02's own 400 m sentence is what routes it there.","evidence_ids":["EV-GPS-00604","EV-TRIP-00604"],"clause_ids":["POL-NS-01","POL-NS-02","POL-NS-03"],"relies_on":"derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count","asserted_weight":1.0},
{"text":"Nothing in either profile supports escalation, and nothing supports treating this driver as a fee-farmer: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1 against completed_trips_30d of 110, a ratio of 0.009, so neither limb of the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check is met; disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both profiles and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, so POL-NS-09(c) and POL-NS-09(d) are not engaged. The case should be decided on the record, not referred, and the driver should not leave it carrying a false-arrival or farming marking.","evidence_ids":["EV-DPROF-00604","EV-RPROF-00604"],"clause_ids":["POL-NS-07","POL-NS-09"],"relies_on":"driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d","asserted_weight":1.0}
]}

