    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee charged on TRP-00604 is refunded in full to the rider.\n\nThe driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-00604, weight 1.0) contains 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes out of 67 fixes; the closest the driver's device came to the Blk 185 pickup pin was 134.62 m and the furthest 302.38 m, against a 50 m STANDARD arrival radius and a 25 m accuracy filter. POL-NS-01 limb (b) therefore fails. Limb (d) also fails: the trip record (EV-TRIP-00604, weight 1.0) shows cancelled_by RIDER with cancellation_reason_code WRONG_PICKUP_LOCATION, not a driver termination on RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT. The anchor clause fails if any single limb breaks, so the SGD 4.00 fee is not chargeable under it. Effective in-geofence dwell was 0 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum (shortfall 300 s), so POL-NS-06 refunds the fee in full; under POL-NS-02 the driver is deemed never to have arrived, and the whole trace sits inside the 400 m ceiling (134.62 m to 302.38 m), which routes the case to POL-NS-03, where the outcome is likewise a full refund of the fee.\n\nDriver compensation is nil. POL-NS-03 allocates fault from the chat log (EV-CHAT-00604, weight 1.0). The rider named the exact sub-location — 'my dad cannot walk, pls come to the block pickup bay Blk 185' at 09:45:50 — and the driver replied 'cannot' at 09:46:20 without moving to that bay before the 09:51:50 cancellation. Under POL-NS-03(i) the driver bears the loss. POL-NS-07 pays nothing because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full, and POL-NS-06 pays nothing where the dwell falls short. The driver's account that he stopped 200 m away is corroborated by the trace (mean displacement 205.90 m) but does not change the result, because the rider had told him where the block bay was.\n\nOn the driver's points: the 09:46:20 reply does defeat any POL-NS-04 exoneration for the rider (limb (b) fails, since the reply came within 120 seconds), but that clause is not the route to this refund, so it does not affect the outcome. The driver's recorded speeds never reach the 15 km/h POL-NS-05 motion trigger and the arrival marker is not shown to be more than 300 m from the pin at the arrival timestamp, so no false-arrival record is written and no referral issues. The chat log contains no abusive message from the driver — the rider's 'got rude' assertion is not supported by the log — but rudeness was never the test for this charge.\n\nNo POL-NS-08 impairment touches any fact this case turns on: the GPS trace has a max gap of 0.0 s at 100% coverage, the chat log's 3 messages match the trip record's chat_message_count of 3 with no msg_id gap, and the SGD 4.00 cancellation line equals the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (4.00). No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: the anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 1 against 110 completed trips in 30 days), and both parties' disputes_with_counterparty_90d and the rider's no_show_disputes_30d are 0. Ratings, account age, lifetime trips and the lifetime counters prior_no_show_flags and prior_deviation_flags are context only under POL-GEN-01 and ground nothing here. Confidence 0.95, capped by the weight-1.0 artifacts that carry the deciding facts.",
